we all have a nostalgic soft spot for  the good old days in Nintendo the Super  Nintendo was my first console and if you  want to use a controller from that era  with a few modern touches 8-bit do has  you covered the SM 30 Pro and the SF 30  Pro are pulled fully featured Wireless  game pads for your switch PC and Android  phones one of these controllers is gonna  run you 50 bucks and you won't be  missing out on any functionality you get  two triggers two bumpers to smooth and  grippy analog sticks that also click  downward all packed into the throwback  mold of the SNES controller sure it  might be weird to see an SNES controller  with analog sticks but these function  really well as you can see the SF 30 Pro  rocks the Super Famicom color scheme  while the SN 30 pro rocks the Super  Nintendo color scheme these also have  motion controls which is a must-have  considering how important it is for  games like Super Mario Odyssey and  splatoon too these connect via bluetooth  and each platform has a different  pairing process that doesn't take too  long these controllers charge through a  USB C 2 USB 2.0 cable and these have  long battery lives on a full charge it  can last up to 16 hours through my  several hours of testing them I never  had to plug them back in off of a full  charge the buttons and analog sticks  feel great to use the triggers in  particular have a short throw but they  are a little on the small side so if you  have big hands it'll be hard to actuate  the classic design of the controller can  also make it a little hard to grip as  long as you clamp the controller tight  enough on both sides this shouldn't be  too much of a problem  I spent time and zelda breath of the  while to get a feel for how the SF 30  pro and the SN 30 pro hold up in a  full-fledged game I didn't have any  issues with how they function and it was  novel playing a 20-17 game with a  throwback gamepad admittedly a pro  controller is more comfortable  especially with the set of triggers and  analog sticks it has I also played a ton  of rocket League for a more intense  twitch based scenario again I had no  issues playing the game and nailing down  shots on goal however if you're super  high level player the precision of a pro  controller is gonna help these  controllers are ergonomically sound  considering they're bottled up to the  Super Nintendo and Super Famicom  controllers but I had one annoyance with  them when the controller vibrates and  makes a high-pitched squealing sound  now if you got headphones on are you  playing a game in a loud room it's not  gonna be a problem but the noise really  picks up in a quiet setting if you want  a fully-featured compact controller for  the Nintendo switch or the PC and you  dig the old-school designs from the SNES  days these are exactly what you're  looking for these aren't going to hold  up to the design of the Nintendo pro  controller and the squeaky vibrations  are kind of annoying but this modern  take on a classic controller from 8-bit  do is on point
 

